# What the formatter must not open.
#
# Prettier also reads .gitignore, so build output, artifacts/, .cache/ and the
# generated fixtures/vault-50/ are already out. This file names the things that
# are tracked and must still be left alone.

# ── Every Markdown file ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Prettier right-pads Markdown table cells to align a column. G41
# (`gate-register`) and G31 (`merge-precedence`) both anchor on an exact single
# space at a pipe, and both extract *nothing* from an aligned table — G41
# silently, caught only by its own vacuous-extraction guard. Measured in #231:
# formatting Markdown turns those two gates red, 3 tests between them.
#
# ⚠️ The protection this leaves standing is markdownlint's MD060 at
# `"style": "compact"` (#251), and only at that style. MD060's default of `any`
# accepts an aligned table, which both regexes are blind to.
*.md

# ── The fixture vault and the cached provider responses ────────────────────
#
# Excluded on fidelity, not on breakage: nothing fails when these are
# formatted. Prettier requotes the YAML frontmatter of 11 vault notes —
# `title`, `author`, `isbn`, `url`, `asin`, `spine_color` — and AGENTS.md's
# adapter contract promises `updateBook` leaves "key order, quoting, comments
# and the note body ... byte for byte" intact. Quoting is named in that
# sentence. The real vault lives outside this repository, so these fixtures are
# the only stand-in for it, and a formatter that reaches them makes them stop
# resembling the thing they are fixtures of.
#
# The same exclusion covers fixtures/api/ — reformatting a recorded API
# response is the same category of error as reformatting a note.
fixtures/

# ── Generated ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
pnpm-lock.yaml
